`export default <expression>` lines: a call prints its callee with `(…)`, objects and arrays print as `{…}` and `[…]` (`{}` and `[]` when empty), an arrow function prints its signature, and parentheses and `as`/`satisfies` don't change what is exported.
Any other expression prints as `export default …`. An identifier is a re-export and prints as written.
== args
input/config.ts
input/empty.ts
input/arrow.ts
input/other.ts
input/name.ts
== file input/config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [],
});
== file input/empty.ts
export default {} satisfies Config;
== file input/arrow.ts
export default async (request: Request): Promise<Response> => respond(request);
== file input/other.ts
export default (["a", "b"]);
export default settings.production;
export default create();
== file input/name.ts
export default App;
